         "kind": "text",
         "weight": 1.0,
         "paragraphs": [
          {
           "role": "type.h2",
           "text": "Valuation"
          },
          {
           "role": "type.body",
           "bullet_level": 0,
           "text": "The $11.40 offer implies 1.33x P / TBV against a 1.08x regional median; every standalone method's midpoint ($9.30 to $11.25) is below the offer, and only analyst targets, the precedent set and the synergy case reach above $12.50"
          },
          {
           "role": "type.body",
           "bullet_level": 0,
           "text": "Standalone DDM midpoint of $10.45 at a 9.25% cost of equity; the offer needs 40% cost synergies to be accretive by FY17"
          },
          {
           "role": "type.h2",
           "text": "Strategic fit"
          },
          {
           "role": "type.body",
           "bullet_level": 0,
           "text": "First Niagara is a pure-play commercial lender: 80% of revenue is net interest income versus 55% for KeyBank, which has spent a decade diversifying"
          },
          {
           "role": "type.body",
           "bullet_level": 0,
           "text": "Geographic overlap is limited to western New York and Pennsylvania; no funding-cost or IP benefit"
          },
          {
           "role": "type.h2",
           "text": "Returns and capital"
          },
          {
           "role": "type.body",
           "bullet_level": 0,
           "text": "ROTCE of 9.0% and CET1 of 9.4% both trail KeyBank; the combined entity dilutes tangible book value per share by 11% at close with a 4.5-year earn-back"
          }
         ]
        },
